{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Backend Error Handling Enforcer",
  "description": "Analyzes backend code changes to ensure proper error handling middleware usage, consistent API error responses, secure logging with correlation IDs, and comprehensive test coverage for failure scenarios",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "secure-gate-access/server/src/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/server/routes/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/server/controllers/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/server/middleware/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/server/services/**/*.js"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified backend file for error handling and logging compliance:\n\n1. **Error Handling Patterns**:\n   - Check if new database queries use proper try/catch or asyncHandler wrapper\n   - Verify external API calls have error handling and circuit breaker patterns\n   - Ensure input validation uses Joi schemas with proper error responses\n   - Confirm async functions are wrapped with asyncHandler middleware\n\n2. **API Response Consistency**:\n   - Verify error responses use standardized errorResponse() helper\n   - Check that error codes follow the ERROR_CODES constants\n   - Ensure HTTP status codes match the error type (400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 500)\n   - Confirm success responses use successResponse() helper\n\n3. **Logging Security & Standards**:\n   - Verify logs include request ID/correlation ID from req.requestId\n   - Check that PII is masked using maskEmail(), maskPhone() functions\n   - Ensure sensitive data (passwords, tokens) is not logged\n   - Confirm structured logging with appropriate log levels (error, warn, info)\n   - Verify security events use loggingService.logSecurity()\n\n4. **Test Coverage Requirements**:\n   - Identify new failure paths that need test coverage\n   - Check for tests covering: invalid input, missing authentication, database failures\n   - Verify integration tests for new API endpoints\n   - Ensure error scenarios are tested with proper assertions\n\n5. **Estate Scoping & Security**:\n   - Confirm multi-tenant data access includes estate_id filtering\n   - Verify authentication middleware (authenticateToken, requireRole)\n   - Check CSRF protection for state-changing operations\n\nProvide specific recommendations for any missing patterns and suggest test cases for new failure scenarios. Reference the error-handling.md guidelines for implementation details."
  }
}